0..77 Comment "// What a hand-written Tarski universe refuses. A decode that runs to a quote"
78..154 Comment "// is the quoted type, so a value of another type is refused there; a decode"
155..230 Comment "// over a binder is a type of its own, so a value at `el(c)` does not stand"
231..277 Comment "// at the decode of the arrow from `c` to `c`."
